00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:22.970
Answer me, Suizenji!

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:22.970
I'm sure you've heard 
about yesterday's event.

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:25.890
Because of that incident,
 we are adjourning for the day.

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:27.680
You should all go straight home.

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:37.730
Quiet down!

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:42.450
This decision was made with your safety in mind.

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:45.200
Don't forget that we're in
 a state of emergency.

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:49.110
Make sure you stay at your house and remain alert until the next school day. Understand? {remain alert} {till time 2 come 2 school}

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:50.450
Yes, sir.

00:03:52.570 --> 00:03:56.320
Hey Asaba, Nishikubo. Let's stop off somewhere on the way home.

00:03:56.320 --> 00:03:58.570
But Kawaguchi told us to go straight home.

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:00.710
What are you doing?

00:04:01.150 --> 00:04:04.180
I can't find the mechanical pencil
 that I always use.

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:05.340
Again?

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:08.110
Didn't you lose your eraser and ruler yesterday, too? {missing}

00:04:08.110 --> 00:04:09.020
A-Akiho!

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:12.300
It'll be fine. It's not like a battle's 
going to break out right away.  {not like we're going to get into a war right away} {not going to break out}

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:13.230
Come on, let's go.

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:13.920
All right.

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:16.020
Asaba, get a move on.

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:17.570
O-Okay.

00:04:18.260 --> 00:04:19.530
Iriya!

00:04:25.420 --> 00:04:26.530
What do you want? {want something (from me)?}

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:31.620
I'm going to go do some research.

00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:33.040
Want to come with me?

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:39.610
I'm writing an article for our newspaper about good restaurants.

00:04:39.610 --> 00:04:41.390
There's all sorts of them.

00:04:41.390 --> 00:04:45.220
I'm going to check some of them out,
 and thought you might like to come too.

00:04:45.530 --> 00:04:48.380
Oh, and you don't have to worry about what Kawaguchi said.

00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:52.420
It's a golden opportunity to 
do some research or write an article.

00:04:52.420 --> 00:04:56.470
Even though you're a member of the 
Newspaper Club, you haven't done any of that yet.

00:04:56.470 --> 00:04:59.620
We need to bring you at <i>least</i> 
 up to Asaba's level.

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:03.440
Are you coming or not?

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:06.690
Victory by default. {won by forfeit?} {unearned win}

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:09.100
I'll go.

00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:19.790
Our first stop today is at a bakery.
It's a 10-minute bus ride away.

00:05:24.110 --> 00:05:26.180
Orange Pekoe and a strawberry parfait. {Dei- i don't think we need notes for foods... orange pekoe is black tea}

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:37.480
Same as Akiho. {y}

00:05:39.030 --> 00:05:40.430
This is bad.{not good}

00:05:40.430 --> 00:05:44.100
Couldn't this be considered spying?
Or maybe eavesdropping?

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:45.610
No one's forcing you to stay!

00:06:03.570 --> 00:06:05.170
How does it taste?

00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:07.550
Sweet.

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:15.770
"Mountain Coffee Shop"

00:06:13.710 --> 00:06:15.770
A fist-sized cream puff and a cold-brew coffee.

00:06:16.380 --> 00:06:17.560
Same as Akiho.

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:24.230
"Piccolo's Pasta"

00:06:20.220 --> 00:06:22.780
Spaghetti with mayonnaise and soy sauce,
 and a cream soda.

00:06:22.780 --> 00:06:24.230
Same as Akiho.

00:06:29.260 --> 00:06:32.700
Hold your horses!
 Move it to your own bowl first!

00:06:33.340 --> 00:06:35.910
They call this "research"?

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:38.340
I'm getting indirect heartburn.

00:06:38.340 --> 00:06:40.730
I've heard girls have a second stomach,
 but this is ridiculous. {I know this rendering is a little long, but I couldn't resist the chance to use this structure.}

00:06:40.730 --> 00:06:42.500
We're not ALL like Akiho!{Don't associate me with Akiho} {lump us all w A}{"issho ni shinaide" is one of those stock phrases that you hear all the time, so I decided to tweak it.}

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:48.670
{You know... // captain no-context}By the way...

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:52.880
Why didn't you come to the school festival?

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:59.070
You totally should've come.

00:06:59.070 --> 00:07:02.450
It was sooooo much fun!

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:08.220
As for me? I helped put out a special edition 
of the newspaper,

00:07:08.220 --> 00:07:11.350
and then went around doing interviews and research with Asaba.

00:07:11.640 --> 00:07:14.330
Did you know about the special edition?
 I bet you didn't!

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:18.250
Anyway, Asaba and I ate yakisoba and some baked potatoes together,

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:20.730
and <i>then</i> we danced at the bonfire together...

00:07:19.740 --> 00:07:20.730
That's a lie.

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:26.440
That last one is... a lie.

00:07:26.440 --> 00:07:27.130
That last one is... a lie.

00:07:36.890 --> 00:07:38.930
Well, let's try one more place.

00:07:39.310 --> 00:07:42.940
You've got room to eat just a bit more, right?

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:45.940
"Iron Man House" {the Marvel character's home?}

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:45.940
This is it. {Here it is}

00:07:50.530 --> 00:07:52.270
Welcome!

00:07:57.550 --> 00:07:58.830
Your order?

00:07:58.830 --> 00:08:00.060
One Iron Man Set. {Ironman meal}

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:00.950
<i>What? {was going to go with "Um, wut?", but then I realized I'm not in gg or subbing a show about penguins.}</i>

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:02.500
Same as Akiho.

00:08:04.760 --> 00:08:09.380
Uh, Miss, I should really explain that our Iron Ma-

00:08:09.390 --> 00:08:10.930
One Iron Man Set!

00:08:10.930 --> 00:08:12.010
Same as Akiho!

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:17.680
"Free Food Challenge - Iron Man Set" 
 (rest of this sign is explained in next scene)

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:17.680
Two challenges coming right up! {IM meals}

00:08:24.930 --> 00:08:28.150
If you can't finish the meal in an hour...

00:08:28.150 --> 00:08:31.670
...or you make an unsightly mess, 
you lose the challenge. {we will end it there}

00:08:31.670 --> 00:08:35.340
It'll set you back 4000 yen. Got it? {fsc}

00:08:35.730 --> 00:08:38.210
You'd better finish at least half of it!

00:08:38.210 --> 00:08:41.330
Remove your hands from the table, and begin!

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:53.970
Hey, they're practically done already!

00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:07.380
What's going on in there?

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:08.280
What's Akiho up to?

00:09:08.280 --> 00:09:09.950
I don't know. I can't see anything. {end on sc}

00:09:10.380 --> 00:09:12.160
Now we have the Iron Man Gyoza.

00:09:10.380 --> 00:09:14.580
Gyoza = dumplings filled with minced pork & vegetables, steamed or lightly pan-fried in oil.

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:14.580
Hands off the table... begin!

00:09:25.550 --> 00:09:26.830
HOT!!!

00:09:28.260 --> 00:09:29.290
Stay back!

00:09:50.880 --> 00:09:52.330
Holy crap!

00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:53.740
It's one hell of a match, isn't it? {is a really good match, huh?}

00:09:53.740 --> 00:09:57.280
Yeah, but keep watching. In the end, the girl with the short hair will win.

00:09:57.280 --> 00:10:01.780
You sure about that? She just looked like she was going to spew all over the place.

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:04.040
Here it comes! 
They're bringing out the Chuukadon!

00:10:02.470 --> 00:10:06.650
Chuukadon = rice topped with meat, vegetables, and seafood, cooked Chinese-style.

00:10:16.710 --> 00:10:20.350
We're changing judges. I'm the boss of this store.

00:10:20.350 --> 00:10:23.640
My family name is Kisaragi,
 and my given name is Juurou.

00:10:23.640 --> 00:10:26.510
Laugh or cry all you want, 
but this is the final course.

00:10:26.510 --> 00:10:28.810
I hope that neither of you 
will come to regret this.

00:10:29.130 --> 00:10:31.930
Now, remove your hands from the table.

00:10:32.990 --> 00:10:34.100
Begin!

00:10:54.950 --> 00:10:56.170
Iriya!

00:10:56.170 --> 00:10:57.070
Miss!

00:10:57.070 --> 00:10:59.660
You idiot! Don't interfere!

00:10:59.660 --> 00:11:01.560
B-But boss!

00:11:01.560 --> 00:11:03.280
Shouldn't we stop this,
 for medical reasons?{AnY-Spork: doctor stop // too literal}

00:11:03.280 --> 00:11:05.370
Don't be such a pansy!

00:11:12.600 --> 00:11:13.730
I won't lose.

00:11:15.290 --> 00:11:18.320
There's no way I'll lose to you, Akiho.

00:11:20.650 --> 00:11:22.320
I definitely... won't lose!

00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:23.320
I definitely... won't lose!

00:11:25.720 --> 00:11:29.350
Thaaaat's perfect!

00:11:32.950 --> 00:11:34.990
Akiho, go for it!

00:11:34.990 --> 00:11:37.010
Iriya, don't lose! Wolf it down!

00:12:02.430 --> 00:12:05.390
Iriya, you awake?

00:12:06.910 --> 00:12:07.900
I am.

00:12:10.760 --> 00:12:11.920
You know...

00:12:15.660 --> 00:12:17.090
I was...

00:12:17.090 --> 00:12:20.840
...afraid of you, Akiho.

00:12:21.930 --> 00:12:24.780
When you asked me to do research with you,

00:12:24.780 --> 00:12:27.540
I was so afraid that my legs started shaking.

00:12:27.540 --> 00:12:32.950
{Lunar: I thought you were going to dump me off where no one else would come and find me.//missed "beat up," other 2 groups got it}I thought you were going to take me to some desolate place and beat me up.

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:39.600
But if I had run away,
 I would have considered it a defeat.

00:12:39.600 --> 00:12:43.110
I was afraid of you,
 but I wasn't going to lose. {no way I could}

00:12:43.110 --> 00:12:45.270
That's what I've always thought.

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:49.990
I've always been afraid of you,

00:12:49.990 --> 00:12:53.410
from the time we first met
 until approximately now.

00:13:01.820 --> 00:13:03.550
What, you guys were awake?

00:13:04.020 --> 00:13:07.270
We brought you some 
stomach medicine. The bitter kind.

00:13:07.270 --> 00:13:08.640
That was incredible.

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:10.760
You two set the record for the youngest to complete the challenge.

00:13:11.880 --> 00:13:15.470
But that was surprising.
 I'll have to call her Nosebleed Kana now.

00:13:15.470 --> 00:13:17.370
What do you mean, "Nosebleed Kana"?

00:13:17.370 --> 00:13:19.690
You guys... were watching us?

00:13:20.270 --> 00:13:22.800
But... how should I put this...

00:13:23.200 --> 00:13:25.250
Let me have that stomach medicine.

00:13:26.420 --> 00:13:28.190
You should take some too, Iriya.

00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:29.910
Okay.

00:13:31.940 --> 00:13:33.730
All right, here you go.

00:13:41.780 --> 00:13:43.670
Who's this old guy?

00:13:45.480 --> 00:13:47.580
Why didn't you call us?

00:13:49.930 --> 00:13:52.060
Why didn't you make the afternoon call?

00:13:53.340 --> 00:13:55.960
Did you have so much fun that you forgot?!

00:13:56.690 --> 00:14:00.090
W-Wait just a second here!
 I made her come along with me.

00:14:01.360 --> 00:14:02.870
We're going back.

00:14:02.870 --> 00:14:04.650
Hold on!

00:14:05.220 --> 00:14:08.280
Who the hell are you, anyway!?

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:12.990
Iriya's Sky

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:12.990
Summer of UFOs

00:14:13.990 --> 00:14:16.960
What? That was Nosebleed Kana's older brother?

00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:19.830
I don't know very much about him.

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:22.800
But he calls himself "Enomoto."

00:14:22.460 --> 00:14:24.800
Sign: "Guts"

00:14:22.800 --> 00:14:24.800
I don't know his given name.

00:14:24.800 --> 00:14:28.270
Then you've met him before?

00:14:28.270 --> 00:14:29.200
Yeah.

00:14:29.200 --> 00:14:32.720
If you actually talk to him, 
you'll see that he's a{ pretty} nice person.

00:14:32.720 --> 00:14:35.610
He's always worried about Iriya. {fsc}

00:14:35.610 --> 00:14:36.770
But why did he...?

00:14:40.710 --> 00:14:42.270
Iriya?!

00:14:57.000 --> 00:15:00.170
Hey, Nosebleed Kana, you've dyed your hair.

00:15:01.070 --> 00:15:03.090
It's platinum blonde, isn't it?

00:15:03.570 --> 00:15:05.420
You look pretty different.

00:15:05.420 --> 00:15:06.380
Yeah, yeah!

00:15:08.130 --> 00:15:10.590
Hey, what are you guys doing?
 Hurry up and take your seats-

00:15:12.580 --> 00:15:13.970
What the hell is that?

00:15:14.620 --> 00:15:17.870
Sensei, its not what you think! 
This is... well...

00:15:17.870 --> 00:15:18.820
Out of my way!

00:15:18.820 --> 00:15:20.940
Hey Iriya, are you trying
 to make a statement here?

00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:23.400
What's with that hair of yours?!

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:25.430
Excuse me, Sensei.

00:15:25.430 --> 00:15:27.860
She didn't exactly dye it.

00:15:27.860 --> 00:15:31.700
Well, I don't know the details, but...

00:15:33.820 --> 00:15:37.810
Oh, that's right! Iriya is always taking a lot of medicines.

00:15:37.810 --> 00:15:40.300
This is probably some sort of side effect.

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:41.880
If that's the case, she can dye it back!

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:44.750
Stand up. We'll continue this
 in the faculty room.

00:15:47.600 --> 00:15:51.220
Iriya Kana-san, you have a call from Tanaka-san. {st?}

00:15:51.220 --> 00:15:56.100
Iriya Kana-san, please come to the faculty room to take the call.

00:15:59.610 --> 00:16:00.730
Let go.

00:16:09.270 --> 00:16:10.360
Iriya!

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:18.750
Don't go. It's only first period!

00:16:19.150 --> 00:16:21.160
Was there even any point
 in coming to school at all?

00:16:22.870 --> 00:16:23.670
There was.

00:16:31.800 --> 00:16:35.430
"Asaba Barbershop"

00:16:32.480 --> 00:16:33.270
Dear?

00:16:33.270 --> 00:16:33.660
Yes?

00:16:33.660 --> 00:16:35.430
Isn't the newspaper a bit... lacking?

00:16:35.750 --> 00:16:38.300
That's all there is,
 and I don't like it one bit.

00:16:38.300 --> 00:16:40.640
It's annoying that we can't even get
 the weather forecast. {can't reseach without news?}

00:16:40.640 --> 00:16:43.850
To the public:

00:16:40.640 --> 00:16:43.850
Currently, information management is being carried out

00:16:40.640 --> 00:16:43.850
in accordance with the New National Defense Act.

00:16:40.640 --> 00:16:43.850
Illegal airwave traffic constitutes a major violation,

00:16:40.640 --> 00:16:43.850
and interferes with emergency preparedness planning.

00:16:40.640 --> 00:16:43.850
Public Safety Squads of the Self-Defense Forces

00:16:40.640 --> 00:16:43.850
will be enforcing the law against pirate broadcasting stations.

00:16:41.320 --> 00:16:43.850
Information control, eh? {that's what you get when the government has control of the information}

00:16:44.960 --> 00:16:49.120
Sakai-san from around the corner dropped by 
to tell me he was going to evacuate.

00:16:50.170 --> 00:16:52.820
It's going to get lonelier around here.

00:16:56.820 --> 00:16:59.200
Quiet Please!

00:16:57.480 --> 00:16:59.200
Huh? Akiho left?

00:16:59.200 --> 00:17:03.660
Nah, she's in the same boat as Hanamura.
Her parents told her to stay home from school.

00:17:04.010 --> 00:17:06.170
{Lunar: But they're counting on you to take care of Iriya. // this makes zero sense in context, were they even watching the show? }But she said to say "hi" to Iriya for her.

00:17:06.780 --> 00:17:09.340
Man, it's like taking care of kindergartners.

00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:33.900
So this is where you were, Iriya.

00:17:36.070 --> 00:17:38.850
Iriya! Can't you tell it's me?

00:17:40.890 --> 00:17:44.420
I can see! I can see just fine!
 I swear I can see!

00:17:44.420 --> 00:17:45.000
Iriya...

